1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,810
A subscription is a product that bills again by itself.

2
00:00:04,810 --> 00:00:10,932
This video shows why subscriptions and memberships exist, how plans, sign-up, agreements and

3
00:00:10,932 --> 00:00:14,680
memberships fit together, and how to use every screen.

4
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:21,741
Some things are not bought once.

5
00:00:21,741 --> 00:00:27,441
Software, courses and clubs charge every month or every year, and customers expect

6
00:00:27,441 --> 00:00:30,420
to start, pause and cancel on their own.

7
00:00:31,170 --> 00:00:36,059
Collecting that by hand means invoices, reminders, and a spreadsheet of who has

8
00:00:36,059 --> 00:00:38,590
paid and who should still have access.

9
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:44,111
A subscription plan is a product that bills again by itself, gives access

10
00:00:44,111 --> 00:00:48,460
to roles while it is paid, and keeps a record of every subscriber.

11
00:00:49,210 --> 00:00:50,908
A membership is simpler:

12
00:00:50,908 --> 00:00:54,699
a product that makes its buyer a member for a number of days,

13
00:00:54,699 --> 00:00:56,170
and ends on its own.

14
00:01:00,370 --> 00:01:04,890
A plan is a content item of a type with the Subscription stereotype.

15
00:01:04,890 --> 00:01:10,020
It has a Product part for its price, and a Subscription part for how it bills.

16
00:01:10,770 --> 00:01:13,806
Plans are listed on a page, such as Plans.

17
00:01:13,806 --> 00:01:19,120
A visitor clicks Sign up, goes through the checkout, and becomes a subscriber.

18
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:27,790
Subscriptions, Agreements lists every subscription, and Subscriptions, My Plans is where a subscriber manages theirs.

19
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:32,768
Commerce, Memberships lists members and their end dates.

20
00:01:32,768 --> 00:01:37,610
Installment plans and sold sites build on the same subscriptions.

21
00:01:41,841 --> 00:01:46,555
A plan type is a content type whose Stereotype is Subscription.

22
00:01:46,555 --> 00:01:52,021
Open Content, Content Definition, Content Types, and edit Membership Plan.

23
00:01:52,476 --> 00:01:56,670
Its parts are the Subscription part, which says how the plan bills, the

24
00:01:56,670 --> 00:02:02,336
Product part, which holds the price, and Subscription Entitlements, which gives subscribers roles.

25
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:07,091
Now open Commerce, Products, and edit the Membership plan.

26
00:02:07,091 --> 00:02:10,855
Billing duration is how often the subscriber pays:

27
00:02:10,855 --> 00:02:13,880
a number, and Year, Month, Week or Day.

28
00:02:14,333 --> 00:02:19,122
Initial amount is a one-time charge at sign-up, named by the Initial amount

29
00:02:19,122 --> 00:02:21,427
description, such as a setup fee.

30
00:02:21,427 --> 00:02:25,683
Billing cycle limit stops the subscription after that many cycles.

31
00:02:26,137 --> 00:02:31,793
Free trial days gives the first days free, while the payment method is still collected.

32
00:02:31,793 --> 00:02:35,077
Subscription day delay starts the billing later.

33
00:02:35,077 --> 00:02:38,787
Under Member access, tick the roles a subscriber holds.

34
00:02:39,251 --> 00:02:42,681
Enter 7 trial days, and click Publish.

35
00:02:46,868 --> 00:02:51,156
The Plans page lists each plan with its price and billing period, and

36
00:02:51,156 --> 00:02:52,471
a Sign up button.

37
00:02:52,471 --> 00:02:53,328
Click it.

38
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:56,050
The checkout begins with the plan.

39
00:02:56,050 --> 00:03:00,137
A visitor who is not signed in is asked to register, and Subscribe

40
00:03:00,137 --> 00:03:03,430
as guest skips the account, when the site allows it.

41
00:03:03,882 --> 00:03:05,263
Click Continue.

42
00:03:05,263 --> 00:03:08,880
On the Payment step, Test payment moves no money.

43
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:13,482
Click Pay now, and the new subscriber lands on the confirmation.

44
00:03:17,684 --> 00:03:23,624
Subscriptions, Agreements lists every subscription, with its plan, its status, how it is

45
00:03:23,624 --> 00:03:26,974
paid, the amount per cycle, and when it renews.

46
00:03:27,428 --> 00:03:30,971
The status drop-down filters the list:

47
00:03:30,971 --> 00:03:36,688
Active, Trial, Past due, Canceled, Expired, Paused or Incomplete.

48
00:03:37,138 --> 00:03:39,643
Click Manage to open a subscription.

49
00:03:39,643 --> 00:03:44,235
It shows its status, what it bills, the current period and its history.

50
00:03:44,235 --> 00:03:49,185
Under Actions, Cancel subscription ends it, and you can choose to Keep access

51
00:03:49,185 --> 00:03:51,153
until the paid period ends.

52
00:03:51,153 --> 00:03:53,718
Pause billing stops charging for now.

53
00:03:57,921 --> 00:04:01,034
Settings, Subscriptions has three settings.

54
00:04:01,034 --> 00:04:05,291
Allow guest sign-up lets people subscribe without an account.

55
00:04:05,744 --> 00:04:10,024
Currency is the default currency of your plans, and the roles you tick

56
00:04:10,024 --> 00:04:13,854
give every new subscriber those roles, whatever plan they buy.

57
00:04:18,058 --> 00:04:21,691
A membership is a product that puts its buyer in roles.

58
00:04:21,691 --> 00:04:26,813
On Annual Membership, under Membership, tick the roles members are in, and enter

59
00:04:26,813 --> 00:04:28,838
the Days a membership lasts.

60
00:04:29,290 --> 00:04:34,137
Commerce, Memberships lists the members with their end dates.

61
00:04:34,137 --> 00:04:39,130
Search by member, and filter by Active, Expired or Ended early.

62
00:04:43,330 --> 00:04:44,640
A software plan:

63
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:49,880
a monthly price, seven free days to try it, and roles that open the paid features.

64
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:52,318
A members-only club:

65
00:04:52,318 --> 00:04:57,450
a yearly plan whose Member role opens articles and guides to subscribers.

66
00:04:58,200 --> 00:04:59,323
A setup fee:

67
00:04:59,323 --> 00:05:03,940
an Initial amount for onboarding, then the regular price each cycle.

68
00:05:04,690 --> 00:05:05,978
A season pass:

69
00:05:05,978 --> 00:05:11,390
a billing cycle limit of three on a monthly plan stops the billing on its own.

70
00:05:13,390 --> 00:05:18,274
Define the plan once, let customers sign themselves up, and keep one list

71
00:05:18,274 --> 00:05:20,562
of who pays and who has access.

72
00:05:20,562 --> 00:05:22,170
Thanks for watching.

